  "steps": [
    {
      "op": "note",
      "text": "FOLD-01 rounds 3 and 4 (Papers, Please 1:1): a paper pressed on the counter follows the pointer one to one onto the desk, in the office view and the reading view, at 1920x1080 and 1280x1024, on days 1 and 12, with full motion and Reduced Motion, and rests with the point that was pressed under the pointer. Each counterDrag presses the paper's visible click box at its middle, near edge or far edge (round 3 pressed its root), drags it at P-SLOW, P-PLAIN, P-FAST or P-FLICK and lets it go mid-mat, at the far corners or near the counter. counterDrag.<name>.follow: the pressed point 8 px or less at 1080p from the pointer on every held frame. .hold: no held frame with the root more than 5 mm from where the pointer asks (G1: the desk surface's clamp; G2: the bound at the back step's lip while the size grows). .rest: on the desk; let go where it lies wholly on the desk once grown, the pressed point rests 8 px or less from the spot under the pointer (G4, FOLD-02); let go before, it slides onto the desk, eased, and rests wholly short of the back step (G3, by design). The drags carry the round 3 verifier's names where they repeat his (o2, o4, o7, r2, r6, r8, r9, c0, e0 to e2). counterdrag.tsv lists every frame."
    },
